  "body": "This is a normative change that requires the ImageData constructor and\nthe createImageData and getImageData methods to rethrow exceptions from\nfrom the creation of the ImageData object. The motivation is to improve\nthe stability of web browsers by avoiding out-of-memory crashes when\nthe creation of ImageData objects fails. The ECMAScript specification\nstates that failure to allocate an ArrayBuffer results in a RangeError\nexception being thrown, which should now be rethrown.\n\nReference:\nhttp://ecma-international.org/ecma-262/6.0/#sec-createbytedatablock\n",
